# The Local Agent Kit ships a scaffold whose `.claude/` contents are CONTENT,
# not repo artefacts. A developer's global excludes file commonly carries
# `**/.claude/settings.local.json` (and `.git/info/exclude` here carries several
# `**/.claude/<file>` rules), which hides them from `git add` — so without these
# negations a fresh clone syncs a kit missing files into the knowledge template:
# a different kit_version and a broken scaffold, silently, for everyone who was
# not the author. The whole directory is negated, not one filename, so a second
# file added to the scaffold's `.claude/` is covered too.
#
# The scaffold's own path-excluding ignore rules ship as dotless `gitignore`
# files (renamed to `.gitignore` by `kit.py new`) precisely so they cannot hide
# scaffold content from this repository the way a nested `.gitignore` would.
!docs/local_agent_kit/templates/agent/.claude/
!docs/local_agent_kit/templates/agent/.claude/**
!backend/app/env-templates/platform-knowledge-env/app/workspace/knowledge/local-kit/templates/agent/.claude/
!backend/app/env-templates/platform-knowledge-env/app/workspace/knowledge/local-kit/templates/agent/.claude/**

# Python bytecode compiled from the Local Agent Kit's `tools/kit.py`. It has no
# rule anywhere today: `backend/.gitignore` scopes `__pycache__`/`*.pyc` to
# backend/ only, and a nested `.gitignore` under docs/local_agent_kit/ is not an
# option — a live one inside that tree hides scaffold content from this repo,
# from the knowledge snapshot and from the contract tarball (see the note above
# about the dotless `gitignore` files). Without these two lines a compiled
# tools/__pycache__/kit.cpython-*.pyc is one `git add -A` away from being
# committed into a tree that is served, and asserted, as UTF-8 text only.
docs/local_agent_kit/**/__pycache__/
docs/local_agent_kit/**/*.pyc

# UI review screenshots (frontend/scripts/ui-shot.mjs)
frontend/.ui-shots/
